        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-0159",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "2 — Containers",
          "documentation": "Inside the pipeline. Every stage is a separately-invoked Node CLI; the stages never call each other — they hand work over through the work directory. The numbers are the order they run in. The build orchestrator is the one thing that runs them: per part of a video, as child processes, before it joins the parts. There are deliberately no arrows between stages, because there are no calls between them.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0160",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "0 · Author",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: author.mjs · Node.js\n\nTurns an observed walk of the app into the DSL. Reads a trace — the selectors found and the wait times measured — and emits the .demo and its selector sidecar together. Sizes the narration to each measured wait, reports any line that will not fit, and proposes a SPEEDS_MS range for whatever narration cannot cover. With --check it re-authors every trace in memory and fails while a committed script differs (pre-commit and CI). Optional: a .demo can be written by hand."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0161",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "1 · Script Compiler",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: script.mjs · Node.js\n\nCompiles a .demo flow into a normal, inspectable scenario module. Refuses to clobber a hand-written scenario. driver.mjs also calls it on the way in."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0162",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "2 · Driver",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: driver.mjs · Node.js + puppeteer-core\n\nLaunches Chrome, signs in if the target says to, runs the flow, and records a screencast plus cursor, click and narration-cue telemetry, plus the real start and end of every wait. Per target it records from its own Chrome profile, keeps chat widgets from loading and hides app banners. Closes Chrome cleanly so cookies flush."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0163",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "3 · Assembler",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: assemble.mjs · Node.js + ffmpeg\n\nTurns frames into raw.mp4 / cut.mp4. Applies CUTS_MS (drop) and SPEEDS_MS (keep, play fast) and puts the cursor and narration telemetry through the same shift, so nothing desyncs. With AUTO_SPEED it fast-forwards every logged wait nobody is talking over. Prints the largest inter-frame gaps."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0164",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "4 · Zoom Projector",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: project.mjs · Node.js\n\nClusters clicks less than 2.5s apart into zoom regions, each carrying a focusTrack the compositor pans across, and writes {take}.recordly."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0165",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "5 · Compositor",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: compose.mjs · Node.js + canvas + ffmpeg\n\nRenders every frame: eased zoom/pan, a synthesized cursor with click ripples, and a styled window frame. Frames stream through ffmpeg both ways; nothing hits disk."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0166",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "6 · Narrator",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: narrate.mjs · Node.js + ffmpeg\n\nVoices the say-cues, trims the breath off each clip, levels every clip to a common loudness, and mixes them onto the video. Extends the video by holding the last frame if a closing line overruns it."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0167",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "7 · Tightener",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: tighten.mjs · Node.js + ffmpeg\n\nCompresses stretches that are frozen AND silent, trims the trailing run, and crossfades every seam. Runs after narrate because silence is only meaningful once the voice is on the timeline. Refuses to write if a seam lands on speech or a zoom. Always writes its output, even with nothing to cut, so the next stage can never pick up an earlier take."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0168",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "8 · Card Renderer",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: cards.mjs · Node.js + canvas + ffmpeg\n\nRenders branded intro/outro title cards, voices them with the same provider, and dissolves them on with the concat filter rather than the demuxer."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0169",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "Flow definitions",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: input/ + scenarios/ authored, scripts/ generated\n\nWhat happens on screen and what is said over it. Split by who writes it: input/ holds the plain-English .flow and scenarios/ the .trace.json observed from walking it, both authored and worth reviewing; scripts/ holds the .demo the trace generates, plus its selector sidecar, either of which can be deleted and rebuilt. Committed; contains no credentials."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0170",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "Targets & secrets",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: targets/*.json, *.local.json, .env\n\nWhich deployment, and how to sign in. The .json is committed and holds no secrets; the .local.json and .env are gitignored. Any value may be written env:VAR_NAME and is read from the environment at load time. A target can also name its own Chrome profile, URLs to block, selectors to hide, and secrets that fill {name} placeholders in an open path."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0171",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "Observed traces",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: scenarios/*.trace.json\n\nWhat the app actually did on a real walk: the selector each step needs, the evidence for it, and how long every wait took. Authored, not generated — it is the only artifact here that cannot be rebuilt from something else, which is why it lives in scenarios/ rather than the gitignored out/. Also carries hazards the DSL cannot yet express, which the author writes into the script header."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0172",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "Selector resolutions",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: scripts/*.selectors.json\n\nWhat each ask description resolved to against the live DOM, plus the evidence for it. Kept beside the script rather than inside it, so the .demo keeps saying what you meant while the machine-found selector stays reviewable on its own. Keyed by intent text, so renaming a selector or reordering the block does not orphan a resolution."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0173",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "Brand assets",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: brand/\n\nStyleGuide.txt (colour and type, the source of truth), the logo, and the font files. One directory is the brand; there is no flag to point elsewhere."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0174",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "Work directory",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: out/ · out/{video}/{part}/\n\nOne folder per take: out/ by default, or out/{video}/{part}/ when the build orchestrator sets DEMO_OUT, so takes never overwrite each other. Holds frames/, frames.json, actions.json, the per-take cursor.json and narration.json, {take}.recordly, the MP4 at each stage (raw, cut, final, final-narrated, -tight, -carded) and the quality gate report with its stills. The hand-off between every stage."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0175",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "TTS clip cache",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: out/tts/ · mp3\n\nOne mp3 per line, keyed by provider+voice+text, plus the derived .lead.mp3 with the opening breath trimmed. Re-cutting or re-composing re-bills nothing; only changed lines re-render. Shared by every take folder."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0176",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "9 · Quality Gate",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: qa.mjs · Node.js + ffmpeg\n\nMeasures what a viewer notices and a stage only warns about: two narration lines at once, a line off its cue, dead air, a frozen or loading screen, black frames, mismatched streams, loudness, and a deliverable built from a previous take. Writes a report and a still per line and per flagged range, and exits 1 on any failure."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0177",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "Build Orchestrator",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: build.mjs · Node.js + ffmpeg\n\nBuilds a whole video from its manifest: records and renders every part into its own folder, gates each on the quality gate, trims the silence at each join by measurement, crossfades the parts and gates the result. Stops at the first failed gate."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0178",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "Video manifests",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: videos/*.json\n\nOne per finished video: its parts in recording order with what must be true before each take, the settings every stage runs with, and how the parts join. Committed."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0179",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "Memory",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0007"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: memory.mjs · Node.js + @getzep/zep-cloud\n\nBookkeeping for project memory: finds the source of each app from .env, diffs a remote listing against the sync lock next to the catalog (files older than the catalog are its baseline), merges new features into the catalog, reports stale sources (SessionStart hook and build.mjs), and pushes changed catalog features, pages, traces and manifests to Zep."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0180",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "Project memory",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: memory/ · committed\n\nrules.md (imported by CLAUDE.md), features/{app}/data/features.json (the feature catalog, the initial set), features/{app}/*.md (one page per filmed feature, naming its videos), sources.json (generic: kinds of source; locations are in .env). A private app folder is gitignored."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-0181",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-0159"
              },
              "name": "Browser profiles",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0008"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: profile/, profile-*/ · gitignored\n\nChrome user-data directories holding signed-in sessions, one per target that needs its own user. Signed in by hand once; a take never signs out. Sensitive: whoever has the folder has the session."
            },
